# CentCompras core

## Project

Central warehouse + satellite branches. Offline-capable product catalogue MVP (Django 6.1, PostgreSQL, plain HTML/JS).

## What exists today

- `accounts` — custom User, email login
- `branches` — Branch, BranchMembership, active branch middleware, `seed_dev_data` command
- `products` — catalogue, staff console `/manage/items/`, admin, audit logs, API, CLI, tests
- `logging_utils` — centralized logging to `logs/`
- **Inbound stock / procurement** — not built; items have no stock field yet
- `orders` — not built; wait until inbound stock exists
- **Tests** — `products/tests.py` (catalogue + console); `accounts` tests for login/groups

## Non-negotiables

- PostgreSQL = source of truth; IndexedDB = read-only catalogue cache
- Branch users: read-only catalogue later; warehouse staff manage items via `/manage/items/` + `products/services.py`
- Business logic in `services.py`; views/commands stay thin
- Branch permissions via `branches/permissions.py`; catalogue via Django groups (`warehouse_admins`, `warehouse_managers`, `warehouse_data_operators`)
- Django admin (`/admin/`) is superuser only; warehouse users work on the website
- Plain Django + plain JavaScript — no React/Vue
- Incremental phases — no large application dumps
- Do not implement the tenancy-doc `Order` stub (`item_name`)
- Do not restyle `/` or polish the staff console unless that session is requested

